course: dictionary
lesson: 10476
title: The tundra: cold, flat and treeless
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The tundra is a huge, cold, flat land with no trees. You find it far in the north, in the Arctic, or high up on mountains. «Snowy owls are wild birds of the Arctic tundra that hunt lemmings.» The word Arctic is a clue that the tundra is in the cold north.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence to work out a new word. «Many tundra animals change clothes with the seasons, the way you swap a summer T-shirt for a winter coat.» The comparison tells you the animals change their colour, like swapping clothes. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: The ground under the tundra stays frozen all year. This frozen ground is called permafrost, so only small plants can grow there, such as mosses, lichens, grasses and small shrubs.
fact: The tundra is a huge, cold, flat, treeless land in the far north or high on mountains.
fact: The ground stays frozen all year. This frozen ground is called permafrost.
fact: Only mosses, lichens, grasses and small shrubs grow on the tundra.
fact: «Lemmings» are small tundra rodents whose numbers rise and fall hugely every few years.
fact: The «arctic fox» and the «ptarmigan» turn white for the snow and brown for the summer ground.
exercise: «Snowy owls are wild birds of the Arctic tundra.» Where is the tundra? | *Far north in the Arctic, or high up on mountains | In the hot desert near the sea | Deep under the ocean | In the middle of big forests
exercise: Which plant can grow on the tundra? | Bamboo | *Mosses | Palm trees | Oak trees
exercise: «The arctic fox and the ptarmigan turn white for the snow.» Find and copy one word that names an animal that changes colour. | summer | *ptarmigan | white | snow
test: What is permafrost? | Deep blue water under the ice | *Ground that stays frozen all year | Hot sand that never cools down | A kind of tall tree
test: Which animal turns white for the snow? | Musk ox | *Arctic fox | Caribou | Lemming
exam: Why does the comparison «swap a summer T-shirt for a winter coat» help a reader? | It explains how to make a winter coat | It tells the reader that the tundra is very hot | It shows that the animals change their colour with the seasons, like changing clothes | *It helps the reader picture animals changing their coats, so the meaning of the sentence becomes clear
